# OPTIONAL: the Jaeger UI (compose.jaeger.yaml) under /jaeger/ on the application's hostname, port
# 443, restricted to operator networks. The site files import /etc/caddy/jaeger-ui.d/*.caddy into
# that site block:
#
#   layout A: https://{$AGENTICWF_HOST}/jaeger/
#   layout B: https://{$AGENTICWF_APP_HOST}/jaeger/
#
# Enable:  sudo mkdir -p /etc/caddy/jaeger-ui.d
#          sudo cp deploy/caddy/jaeger-ui/agenticwf-jaeger-ui.caddy /etc/caddy/jaeger-ui.d/
# Disable: sudo rm /etc/caddy/jaeger-ui.d/agenticwf-jaeger-ui.caddy
# Then:    sudo systemctl reload caddy
#
# Install ONE Jaeger UI file. The others, in /etc/caddy/jaeger-ui-app.d/, serve it inside the
# application (layout A: /app/jaeger/), with Logto sign-in (agenticwf-jaeger-ui-logto.caddy) or
# without (agenticwf-jaeger-ui-network.caddy); README.md, Tracing.
#
# Jaeger serves its UI and API under the same prefix (base_path in deploy/jaeger/jaeger.yaml), so
# the path is passed on unchanged; change both together.
#
# Traces carry request paths, user ids and timings, and Jaeger has no login of its own: access is
# by network, as for the Logto admin console. Caddy environment (no default on purpose):
#   AGENTICWF_ADMIN_ALLOWED_CIDRS="188.184.0.0/15 2001:1458::/32"   # your networks
# If it is unset, everyone gets 403. These requests do not go through authsvc and are not traced.

redir /jaeger /jaeger/ 308

@agenticwf_jaeger_ui path /jaeger/*
handle @agenticwf_jaeger_ui {
	@outside not remote_ip {$AGENTICWF_ADMIN_ALLOWED_CIDRS}
	respond @outside "Forbidden" 403

	request_header -X-Auth-*
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:16686
}
